menu "epdiy (vendored, reflbo patches)"

    config EPD_S3_SHIFT_REGISTER_LATCH
        bool "ESP32-S3 with the panel's latch on a shift register"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        default n
        help
            reflbo patches P2 and P4 (PATCHES.md): epdiy's row-by-row output path, as on the ESP32, with
            each row sent over LCD_CAM's i80 bus. For boards whose LE and STV come from a shift register,
            as the LilyGo T5-ePaper-S3 V2.3's 74HCT4094, so the LCD path's HSYNC latch can't be used.

    config EPD_LUT_IN_PSRAM
        bool "Waveform LUT in PSRAM"
        default n
        help
            reflbo patch P5: the 64 KB conversion LUT in PSRAM instead of internal RAM. Slower, but it
            leaves internal RAM to Wi-Fi. Without it, a failed internal allocation falls back to PSRAM.

endmenu
